# V4d: one of FIVE runs (V4a..V4e), each after its own all-four reset, of the AUDITS-OFF hang shapes on c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace-v5: the production recipe (audits off, the pinned
# sampler recorded in the verify trace, the tail caps) plus the split recurrence launch. The split launch adds one semaphore to the verify trace, and the trace shape of production is safe
# only by layout: FIVE CONSECUTIVE COMPLETIONS are the evidence; one stall restarts the count, stops the window and leaves the cards hung until the hand-back's reset.
# Read: every test completes, no stall-watch stack dump, the engaged line, '[PINDIAG] four-card engine programs=' deltas small after the captures, no late prefill program.
# STOP on a stall, a hang or a refusal. Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min, build 10-20 min on a warm cache, the shapes 15-20 min: 40 min per run.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/v5split window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/v5split and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (the tag numbers are the driver's, on the
# allowlist). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is
# pushed from this branch.
# TWO IMAGES: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-1 (a PLACEHOLDER the driver substitutes) is the build the single-card byte gate runs in (the gate mounts this
# checkout's scripts, so any current C2 image carries the runtime it needs); C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-2 is the build of the commit that adds the
# qualified sha256 triple (gdn_seq_block_split.QUALIFIED), which the four-card jobs serve. A reused tag is skipped by the build step.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-v5split-2
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace-v5
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_v164order,concurrent4_steady,replay_concurrent4
